              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹೊಂದಿಕೊ (hondiko) is native Dravidian: hondu, \"to join, come together\", which DEDR 4541 lists, and ko, from koḷḷu, \"to take\" (DEDR 2151), which turns the action back on the doer: \"to fit oneself in\". DEDR 4541 compares, with a query, Prakrit pora."
